// plain identifiers, so ident runs after the `<` are exactly the names.
//
// The identifier CHARACTER CLASS is `tyname.nameIdentChar` (W8), shared with
// `modTypeRenamed` below. The RUN WALK stays here, and that is a MEASUREMENT rather than a
// preference: the census's proposed home was a run TOKENIZER
// (`nameIdentRuns(name, outStart, outEnd)`), it was built, this site was routed to it, and
// the compiler grew **608 bytes** — two materialised `i32[]` index columns and their push
// loops, to serve the tokenizer's ONE legal consumer (`modTypeRenamed` cannot take it; see
// its header). The classifier is the operation that is actually written twice; the walk is
// written once, and moving a single writing changes its location, not the count.
//
// The `<` is FOUND rather than walked past, which retires the copy's `started` flag: that
// flag was only ever "have I passed the first `<` yet", and starting at `lt + 1` answers it
// positionally. A trailing run is flushed by the closing `>`, as in the copy — every
// declared generic name ends in one.
function modGenParams(name: string): string[] {
